`unorm_dart` is pinned exactly at **0.3.1+1** because that is the Unicode 16.0 release the design settled on — 0.3.2 (current pub.dev latest) moved to Unicode 17.0, and a caret would float to it. The dependency demanded no further file changes, so no STOP was needed.

## What D0 delivers (`src/cljc/yin/vm/debruijn.cljc`)

- **Dimension descriptor** — d3 subgraph `descriptor` with `:dim/arity 22`, the §4 slots in declared order (`dimension-slots`, with the `[:ordered-vector :ref]` type for operands), `:dim/encoding` (sha256, descriptor slot order, the two hash-excluded marker slots, embedded canonical-value table), `:dim/projection-to` d1+d3, `:dim/lift-from` d5. `dimension-hash` = content hash of that subgraph — the published domain separator, not an ad hoc string.
- **Canonical value table** as data (`canonical-value-table`, symbolic bounds so the descriptor prints identically on every host) plus `canonical-class`/`canonical-value?` validation implementing §5's numeric rules: int64 for exact host integers and in-range integral doubles (1 ≡ 1.0), one quiet-NaN class, distinct signed zeros, and §5's JavaScript carve-out — a CLJS unsafe integral is a diagnostic; JVM/CLJD classify in-range integral doubles as int64 (documented host divergence for D3's cross-host fixtures to arbitrate). Bigints, ratios, chars, decimals diagnose.
- **One NFC seam** `normalize-nfc`: `java.text.Normalizer` / `String.prototype.normalize("NFC")` (uppercase — lowercase throws RangeError on Node) / `unorm_dart`'s `nfc`.
- **Root framing & validation per §2**: `frame-datoms` (marker closes the graph, per-frame fact-index reset for -16-restarting tempids, `:partial-frame` at end of stream) and `project-datoms` (exactly-one-root, assert-only via `dao.datom/reserved`'s `:db/retract` — any other m valid and dropped with t from identity, other namespaces ignored, `:yin/tail?`/`:yin/macro-name` tolerated-and-ignored, unknown `:yin/*` on walked nodes, duplicates, dangling refs, cycles, unknown types, unexpanded-macro lambda-operator rule with the registry-macro limit documented, unsupported values).
- **`node-grammar`** — the §2 table as the walk vocabulary with fixed child order.

**D1**: `resolve-name` (depth 0 innermost, leftmost position 0, inner-to-outer, right-to-left rightmost-wins — parity-asserted against `engine/bind-params`), and the projection walk returning `{:root node}` with `:yin.debruijn/*` slots — bound occurrences as `{:bound [depth position]}`, free as `{:free name}`, binders as arities — memoized by `[source-eid complete-frame-stack]`, **no hashing** (the only digest in the file is the D0 domain separator).

